{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2223","id":5285005068,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOwLHDA","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2223","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2223.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2223.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2223","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2223/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2223/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2223/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/8752357228cdc9650b5b7cc5f2383b61a8fdb7d8","number":2223,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-1776: the demo-user seed timer in services/auth catches a synchronous throw and logs it","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs KS-1776\n\nLinear ticket: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-1776\n\n**BLUF:** Tier 2. Importing `services/auth/src/routes/auth.ts` arms a module-scope 2000 ms `setTimeout` that calls `userRepo.seedDemoUsers(hashPassword).catch(...)`. The `.catch` handled a rejection only; a SYNCHRONOUS throw from the call (a repository mock that lacks the export, a repository that is not ready) escaped the timer as an uncaught exception, which the test runner pins on whichever test is running. The call now sits in a `try/catch` and both the throw and the rejection go to one shared `logSeedFailure`, which writes the same `Failed to seed demo users` line as before. Ten added lines and three removed in `Blockchain/Dev/services/auth/src/routes/auth.ts` (develop `1dd6299bccd6`) plus one new test file. No auth decision, token, credential, database write or response changes; the seed itself is unchanged.\n\n## What changes\n- **Product, `routes/auth.ts` (+10 -3):** a `logSeedFailure` helper with a why-and-ticket comment, and the timer's call wrapped in `try { ... .catch(logSeedFailure) } catch (err) { logSeedFailure(err) }`. The timer, its 2000 ms delay and the log message are unchanged.\n- **New cell file, `Blockchain/Dev/services/auth/src/__tests__/ks1776-demo-user-seed-timer-cannot-escape-as-an-uncaught-throw.test.ts` (102 lines, 4 cells, fake timers):** drives the real routes module with the repository mocked. D1: firing the timer does not throw when the repository has no `seedDemoUsers`. D2: the missing export is logged as `Failed to seed demo users`. Control C1: with `seedDemoUsers` present it is called once, with the password hasher, after 2000 ms and not before. Control C2: a `seedDemoUsers` that rejects is still logged.\n- The fix shape is the held patch's (the ticket proposes none): a local-model queue patch applied unmodified. Its added and removed lines are byte-identical to the held ready file's, the applied tree's changed lines per file equal the patch's, and git applied it with its own offset of 3 lines on the one hunk and nothing else.\n- Open PRs: none touches `routes/auth.ts` (census at the push).\n\n## Red, green (measured on this tree's bytes)\n- The new cell file alone, against develop's unchanged product: 2 failed (D1, D2: the timer call throws `No \"seedDemoUsers\" export is defined on the \"../repositories/userRepo\" mock`) and 2 passed (the controls). With this change: 4 of 4.\n- **Whole `services/auth` suite, run N times before and after (N = 5 interleaved pairs, before then after, so load drift hits both sides alike; load1 3 to 18 while two other jobs ran):** before the change 156 files and 1,883 tests, exit status 0 in 5 of 5 runs; after the change 157 files and 1,887 tests (the four new cells), exit status 0 in 5 of 5. The intermittent exit 1 with every test green that this ticket's comment of 2026-11-11 records (3 of 4 pristine-develop runs) and that PR 2216's body names did NOT reproduce in any of my 10 runs, so these runs show no effect of this change on it, in either direction. This PR claims the cell above, not a cure for that flake.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n- **Touched:** `services/auth` only: one product file and one new test file. No fragment pair added: the docs-fragments check passes without one (measured).\n- **Ran** (Node v26.8.1, not the Node 24 LTS line; one Apple Silicon host; vitest through `npm test -- run` in the package): the new cell file red and green; the whole suite 5 times before and 5 times after as above; `docs-fragments.mjs check`: OK (244 new, unchanged by this PR); eslint on the two changed files (absolute paths, the repo's root flat config): 0 errors, 0 warnings; `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.test.json` for the package: rc 2 on develop's existing diagnostics (26 distinct sites), none in the two changed files.\n- **NOT run:** any other service's suite; the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6); Docker or the compose stack; a real service start; Node 24. The pre-merge acknowledgement boxes for Schemathesis and Akto are therefore NOT ticked.\n- **Migrations + config:** none.\n- **Pre-push hook:**\n\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 127 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 127)`\n\n## Before this deploys\nNothing deploys from this PR. The change is a catch around a startup timer in the auth service, so it takes effect only after the auth image is rebuilt and the service redeployed; no migration, config or secret changes, and no API, schema or data change.\n\n## Not claimed\nThat this removes the intermittent whole-suite exit status (it did not reproduce in my runs), any other timer or startup call, the seeder itself and the test mocks that lack the export. This PR selects the ticket's identified timer; it does not claim the ticket is done.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T20:52:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T20:52:11Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"39d2f95e9a75f674de2d17871367a423af6a68a2","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-1776-demo-user-seed-timer-cannot-escape-as-an-uncaught-throw","ref":"feature/ks-1776-demo-user-seed-timer-cannot-escape-as-an-uncaught-throw","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sec